From c3e9a6558953584abd03a2af835b9c860955415a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:09:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pin every action to a commit, with its version beside it

A workflow that names a moving tag runs whatever the tag points to on the
day it runs, so a release of claude-code-action or of GitHub's own actions
reached every run here, and every copy, the day it was published, without
review. Each of the 30 uses: lines now names the commit its tag pointed to
on 2026-10-14 (checkout v7.0.1, upload-artifact v7.0.2, cache v6.1.0,
create-github-app-token v1.12.0, claude-code-action v1.0.249), with the
version in a comment, which Dependabot reads to propose the next commit.

Dependabot now groups every action into one pull request a week: with
commit pins it proposes every patch release, and claude-code-action ships
several a week, so one group keeps that to one review. The writing rule and
the GitHub setup page say "pinned to a commit" instead of "pinned to a major
tag", and a new test holds every workflow to it: a tag, a pin without its
version comment, or one action pinned to two commits fails the check.

This is the first pull request of the plan the owner approved on
2026-10-14 (/mnt/project-files/plans/gh-aw-migration-plan.md, section 6,
PR 1a). Nothing else changes: the same commits run as ran today.

